From 88f809911806d6f27f0165d67c42f45efea1a946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:39:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: Hades' strings in a block of their own, 20000 above
 their ids

Kodi's master uses #39220 and #39221 for strings of its own, which
Hades used too, and Kodi's core strings reach 40866 and grow from
there, towards the ids that Hades took from 40920 on; Hades' strings
of Estuary started at 31616, which Estuary in Kodi's master uses now.
Every string of Hades (an id that Kodi's Piers branch does not have)
moves up by 20000: the core ones from 39220-42261 to 59220-62261,
Estuary's from 31616-34261 and 41170-41923 to 51616-54261 and
61170-61923, so one rule reads any number written before. Kodi's skin
range 31000-31999 is left to Kodi: an Estuary string of Hades that was
in it is reached as $ADDON[skin.estuary n] instead of $LOCALIZE[n]. In
the core file the strings of Hades leave Kodi's part, which is the file
of the Piers branch again, line for line, for one block at its end.
Texts, translations and comments are the same; only the ids change,
in the .po files, the XML, the settings and the code that names them.
