 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #39881)
-msgctxt "#32111"
+#. Setting help: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #59881)
+msgctxt "#52111"
 msgid "On (the default): sound that Hades decodes goes out in no more channels of PCM than your display says it takes (read from its EDID), whatever 'Number of channels' says. A TV that declares stereo gets stereo, and one that declares 6 channels gets 5.1. A display that declares PCM of 16 or 20 bits only gets 16 bits. This avoids silence from sound that the display cannot take. Off: decoded sound follows 'Number of channels' alone, in as many bits as the output offers, for a display that takes more than it declares. Passthrough is not affected."
 msgstr ""
 
