 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #40921)
-msgctxt "#32095"
+#. Setting help: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #60921)
+msgctxt "#52095"
 msgid "Dolby Vision films carry the colourist's trims: small corrections that say how each scene should look on a display of a few given peak brightnesses (100, 600 or 1000 nits, for instance). When your TV does Dolby Vision itself (native output), the TV applies the trims on its own, and this decides whether they are sent to it. Off (the usual): they are sent. On: they are not; turn it on only if the TV shows washed-out blacks or wrong colours because of them, as some projectors do. Where LibreELEC Hades adjusts Dolby Vision to your display itself (shown as HDR10 adjusted to the display, as SDR, or in Low-Latency), it applies the trims only if \"Dolby Vision: apply the trims when adjusting to your display\" is on, and never while this is on. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr "Las películas Dolby Vision llevan los trims del colorista: pequeñas correcciones que dicen cómo debe verse cada escena en pantallas de unos pocos brillos máximos (100, 600 o 1000 nits, por ejemplo). Cuando tu TV hace el Dolby Vision ella misma (salida nativa), la TV aplica los trims por su cuenta y esto decide si se le envían. Desactivado (lo normal): se le envían. Activado: no; activalo solo si la TV muestra negros lavados o colores equivocados por su causa, como hacen algunos proyectores. Donde LibreELEC Hades adapta él mismo el Dolby Vision a tu pantalla (mostrado como HDR10 adaptado a la pantalla, como SDR o en Low-Latency), solo aplica los trims si «Dolby Vision: aplicar los trims al adaptar a tu pantalla» está activado, y nunca mientras este esté activado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting label: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40922)
-msgctxt "#32096"
+#. Setting label: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #60922)
+msgctxt "#52096"
 msgid "Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision"
 msgstr "Reproducir videos HDR10+ como Dolby Vision"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40923)
-msgctxt "#32097"
+#. Setting help: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #60923)
+msgctxt "#52097"
 msgid "For a TV that supports Dolby Vision but not HDR10+. An HDR10+ video is sent as Dolby Vision, with metadata made from its own HDR10+ data, scene by scene (the peak and the average brightness of each scene). The picture is the same HDR10 picture. What does not carry over from HDR10+: the tone curve and the target display that the studio chose, its saturation weight and its windows; in Dolby Vision Low-Latency (game mode), where Hades adapts each picture to the TV itself, the studio's tone curve is applied. Dolby Vision videos, HDR10 videos without HDR10+ and displays that take HDR10+ are not affected. Off by default. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr "Para una tele compatible con Dolby Vision pero no con HDR10+. Un video HDR10+ se envía como Dolby Vision, con metadatos hechos a partir de sus propios datos HDR10+, escena por escena (el brillo máximo y el medio de cada escena). La imagen es la misma imagen HDR10. Lo que no pasa de HDR10+: la curva de tonos y la pantalla de referencia que eligió el estudio, su peso de saturación y sus ventanas; en Dolby Vision Low-Latency (modo juego), donde Hades adapta cada imagen a la tele, se aplica la curva de tonos del estudio. Los videos Dolby Vision, los HDR10 sin HDR10+ y las pantallas que admiten HDR10+ no se ven afectados. Viene desactivado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting label: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40924)
-msgctxt "#32098"
+#. Setting label: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #60924)
+msgctxt "#52098"
 msgid "Make HDR10 videos Dolby Vision (measured)"
 msgstr "Convertir videos HDR10 a Dolby Vision (medido)"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40925)
-msgctxt "#32099"
+#. Setting help: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #60925)
+msgctxt "#52099"
 msgid "For a TV that supports Dolby Vision. An HDR10 video has no Dolby Vision data of its own, so Hades measures the picture as it plays (the peak, the average and the darkest level of each scene, and the black bars) and sends that as Dolby Vision metadata. These are not the studio's data: nothing of a colourist's grade (trims) is added. Scene cuts are found from the picture: a few are missed, a few are found where there is none, and some are found a picture late. The picture itself is the same HDR10 picture. Dolby Vision and HDR10+ videos are not affected. Off by default. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr "Para una tele compatible con Dolby Vision. Un video HDR10 no tiene datos Dolby Vision propios, así que Hades mide la imagen mientras se reproduce (el máximo, el promedio y el nivel más oscuro de cada escena, y las barras negras) y lo envía como metadatos Dolby Vision. No son los datos del estudio: no se añade nada de la calibración de un colorista (trims). Los cortes de escena se detectan por la imagen: algunos se pierden, algunos se detectan donde no hay, y otros con una imagen de retraso. La imagen es la misma imagen HDR10. Los videos Dolby Vision y HDR10+ no se ven afectados. Viene desactivado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting label: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+ (core #40926)
-msgctxt "#32100"
+#. Setting label: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+ (core #60926)
+msgctxt "#52100"
 msgid "Send it as HDR10+ where the display takes it"
 msgstr "Enviarlo como HDR10+ donde la pantalla lo admite"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+ (core #40927)
-msgctxt "#32101"
+#. Setting help: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+ (core #60927)
+msgctxt "#52101"
 msgid "For a display that takes HDR10+ but not Dolby Vision, as many Samsung TVs. A Dolby Vision video rebuilt as HDR10 is sent as HDR10+, with scene-by-scene metadata that Hades measures from the rebuilt picture, so that the display adapts each scene as it does with an HDR10+ film. These data are not the studio's and no tone curve is sent: the display makes its own, and may show a scene differently from plain HDR10. Profile 8.1 is then rebuilt too. Not used while the picture is mapped to the display. For one video, the video settings of the player can send it as plain HDR10 or as HDR10+. Off by default. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr "Para una pantalla que admite HDR10+ pero no Dolby Vision, como muchas teles Samsung. Un video Dolby Vision reconstruido como HDR10 se envía como HDR10+, con metadatos escena por escena que Hades mide de la imagen reconstruida, para que la pantalla adapte cada escena como con una película HDR10+. Esos datos no son los del estudio y no se envía curva de tonos: la pantalla usa la suya y puede mostrar una escena distinta del HDR10 normal. El perfil 8.1 también se reconstruye. No se usa mientras la imagen se mapea a la pantalla. Para un video, los ajustes de video del reproductor pueden enviarlo como HDR10 normal o como HDR10+. Viene desactivado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #. Hades, the Dolby Vision page of the player information: a Dolby Vision picture rebuilt and sent as HDR10+, with dynamic metadata measured from it
-msgctxt "#32102"
+msgctxt "#52102"
 msgid "Dolby Vision rebuilt, sent as HDR10+ (metadata measured by Hades)"
 msgstr "Dolby Vision reconstruido, enviado como HDR10+ (metadatos medidos por Hades)"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting label: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #39880)
-msgctxt "#32110"
+#. Setting label: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #59880)
+msgctxt "#52110"
 msgid "Limit PCM to what the display declares"
 msgstr "Limitar el PCM a lo que declara la pantalla"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #39881)
-msgctxt "#32111"
+#. Setting help: the channels of PCM limited to what the display declares (core #59881)
+msgctxt "#52111"
 msgid "On (the default): sound that Hades decodes goes out in no more channels of PCM than your display says it takes (read from its EDID), whatever 'Number of channels' says. A TV that declares stereo gets stereo, and one that declares 6 channels gets 5.1. A display that declares PCM of 16 or 20 bits only gets 16 bits. This avoids silence from sound that the display cannot take. Off: decoded sound follows 'Number of channels' alone, in as many bits as the output offers, for a display that takes more than it declares. Passthrough is not affected."
 msgstr "Activado (lo predeterminado): el sonido que decodifica Hades sale en no más canales de PCM de los que tu pantalla dice admitir (leído de su EDID), diga lo que diga 'Número de canales'. Una tele que declara estéreo recibe estéreo, y una que declara 6 canales recibe 5.1. Una pantalla que solo declara PCM de 16 o 20 bits recibe 16 bits. Así se evita el silencio con sonido que la pantalla no puede admitir. Desactivado: el sonido decodificado sigue solo 'Número de canales', con tantos bits como ofrezca la salida, para una pantalla que admite más de lo que declara. El paso directo (passthrough) no se ve afectado."
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting label: decoded surround as Dolby for a display of stereo PCM (core #39882)
-msgctxt "#32112"
+#. Setting label: decoded surround as Dolby for a display of stereo PCM (core #59882)
+msgctxt "#52112"
 msgid "Surround as Dolby when the display takes only stereo PCM"
 msgstr "Envolvente como Dolby cuando la pantalla solo admite PCM estéreo"
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Setting help: decoded surround as Dolby for a display of stereo PCM (core #39883)
-msgctxt "#32113"
+#. Setting help: decoded surround as Dolby for a display of stereo PCM (core #59883)
+msgctxt "#52113"
 msgid "For a display that declares PCM in 2 channels only, but takes Dolby Digital Plus or Dolby Digital in more. A surround track that Hades decodes (DTS where the display does not take it, or any track whose passthrough is off) is then encoded to Dolby Digital Plus 5.1 (Dolby Digital 5.1 where the display does not declare Dolby Digital Plus, its passthrough is off or the output does not take its rate) and passed through, so the sound stays surround. The encoding is lossy (768 kb/s; 640 kb/s for Dolby Digital), and 7.1 is mixed down to 5.1. Off, or where neither can be sent: it is mixed down to stereo. Needs passthrough and Dolby Digital passthrough on."
 msgstr "Para una pantalla que declara PCM solo en 2 canales, pero admite Dolby Digital Plus o Dolby Digital en más. Una pista envolvente que decodifica Hades (DTS donde la pantalla no lo admite, o cualquier pista cuyo passthrough esté desactivado) se codifica entonces a Dolby Digital Plus 5.1 (Dolby Digital 5.1 donde la pantalla no declara Dolby Digital Plus, su passthrough está desactivado o la salida no admite su frecuencia) y se pasa directa, así que el sonido sigue siendo envolvente. La codificación tiene pérdidas (768 kb/s; 640 kb/s en Dolby Digital) y el 7.1 se reduce a 5.1. Desactivado, o donde no se puede enviar ninguno: se reduce a estéreo. Necesita el passthrough y el passthrough de Dolby Digital activados."
 
